Fix uninitialized variable in glTF2 import test

The shadingMode variable was declared but not initialized. If material->Get()
fails, shadingMode would be used uninitialized in the subsequent EXPECT_EQ.
This triggers -Werror=maybe-uninitialized with certain compiler configurations.

Initialize to aiShadingMode_Flat as a safe default.

--- a/test/unit/utglTF2ImportExport.cpp
+++ b/test/unit/utglTF2ImportExport.cpp
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ class utglTF2ImportExport : public ::testing::Test {
         const aiMaterial *material = scene->mMaterials[0];

         // This Material should be a PBR
-        aiShadingMode shadingMode;
+        aiShadingMode shadingMode = aiShadingMode_Flat;
         EXPECT_EQ(aiReturn_SUCCESS, material->Get(AI_MATKEY_SHADING_MODEL, shadingMode));
         EXPECT_EQ(aiShadingMode_PBR_BRDF, shadingMode);

